tinyalsa/  --  NAVER Corporation, BSD-style
------------------------------------------------------------------

    asoundlib.h

Despite the directory name this is NOT tinyalsa upstream code and no
tinyalsa copyright applies to it.  It is a 29-line stub written at NAVER
that declares only the pcm_format enumeration and the
pcm_format_to_bits() helper the HAL needs at compile time; the real
symbols are resolved against the container's libtinyalsa.so at runtime.
It carries the same BSD-style header as the rest of our sources.


Binary distribution
------------------------------------------------------------------

For the shipped audio.primary.cras.so the same attribution is carried on
the about:credits page through the AOSP-audio-headers custom license in
chromiumos-overlay/licenses/, listed in the ebuild's LICENSE field.
